The page remembers where the member left the companion on this device, as A-NAS's spec
asks (docs/specs/virtual-companion.md); dsh-pet's card keeps its position for the page's
life only (customPos starts empty). Every move that ends sets that position, whether a drag,
a flight, a walk, a position command or the window's new size, so the card now tells the
page each new one through the `onPlace` prop. The page puts a remembered position back with
an instant position command, the card's own way to place the pet.

